cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CrediTAD, please cite it as below."
title: "CrediTAD: structured per-boundary evidence records for post-calling review of TAD boundaries"
abstract: >-
  A downstream evidence-audit workflow for already-called Hi-C TAD boundaries. For each
  candidate boundary supplied by any caller, CrediTAD records cross-caller support (BD1)
  and three separate molecular readouts - CTCF ChIP (BD2), RAD21/cohesin ChIP (BD3) and
  chromatin-loop anchors (BD4) - as separately graded fields, keeps an unmeasured axis
  distinct from a measured-and-unenriched one, and combines them with a deterministic,
  inspectable rule into a D1-D5 evidence tier. The tier is not a probability and not a
  ground-truth label. CrediTAD does not call TADs and does not rank callers.
type: software
